          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "**Use a client-side SPA.** For a dashboard behind a login, SSG and ISR give you nothing. They pre-render public, cacheable pages, and your content is per-user and has no SEO value. SSR's main payoffs, crawlable HTML and a fast first paint of public content, don't apply either.\n\n- **SPA (Vite + React/Vue, or similar):** This is the simplest option. You get static hosting on a CDN, a fast app shell, and all the data from your API with auth tokens or cookies. Interactive, data-heavy UIs are what SPAs do well.\n- **SSR is worth it only if** you need to avoid a loading-spinner waterfall on first load, want server-side auth checks before any HTML ships, or already run Next.js or Remix for a public marketing site. In that case, keep the marketing pages static or SSR'd and the dashboard client-rendered.\n\nPut the marketing site and login page on SSG if you have them, and keep the dashboard itself a plain SPA."
        },
