          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "**There's no single right stack. This is the default I'd pick:** TypeScript everywhere, with React and Next.js (App Router) for UI and server rendering. Use Postgres for data, Vite if you don't need SSR, and deploy on Vercel or Docker behind Nginx.\n\n- **Language:** TypeScript on both client and server. Validate inputs with zod.\n- **Rendering:** Choose per route. Use static pages for content, SSR or React Server Components for dynamic pages, and client-side islands for heavy interactivity.\n- **State:** Keep server state (TanStack Query or RSC) separate from UI state.\n- **Ops:** Use HTTPS, CI with tests before deploy, and Playwright for e2e.\n\nTwo cases change this:\n- **Mostly content:** Use static generation with Astro or Next plus a CDN.\n- **Team already knows Vue or a different backend:** Use that instead, since team familiarity matters more than fashion.\n\nTell me what the app does, who the users are, and what your team knows, and I'll narrow it down."
        },
